      "side": 1,
      "message": "AIUI, TestNetworkService is never stopped. Therefore it should simply never removes the policy change listener. You can have a comment on the add() method if you want. I don\u0027t think it\u0027s helpful to have a remove() just to have a remove(), if we\u0027re never actually going to remove it.\n\nI think the current code with the finalizer is not even correct, because really if you want to have something that follows the lifecycle correctly then you\u0027ll want to remove the listener when the last ref to TestNetworkService is lost, because then you no longer want to look up the members. Generally finalizers are hard to use and are almost never the right solution.\n\nJust remove the finalizer.",
