      "writtenOn": "2021-05-12T08:45:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What is the threading model for this mutable member (and the one below ?)\nIt\u0027s not accessed locked, and it\u0027s accessed on the handler thread in the VCN policy listener, and in some other thread (guaranteed to be different) in the constructor of NetworkAgent. That means some percentage of the time you\u0027ll see null and crash the system server in l.499.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 201,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 201,
        "endChar": 66
      },
      "revId": "8d604fe6360528ab63c60f9e3ec9d7e9e96bd747",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c19a841e_b1e6f67d",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/TestNetworkService.java",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 201,
      "author": {
        "id": 1463964
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-05-13T01:55:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "for mLinkProperties: it is now final, so nullness should not be a concern there.\n\nfor mNetworkCapabilities: I\u0027m not sure null is ever possible - the value starts as non-null and nullness is checked when the NetworkCapabilities is updated in updateNetworkCapabilities() so it will stay non-null.\n\nIn the constructor, the field is only set which runs on the binder thread. It is read+set in the policy listener on TestNetworkService\u0027s handler thread, but this is synchronized on mTestNetworkTracker. \n\nIs this sufficient, or should more explicit locking on this field be added?",
      "parentUuid": "5175d034_f5846552",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 201,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 201,
        "endChar": 66
      },
      "revId": "8d604fe6360528ab63c60f9e3ec9d7e9e96bd747",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3a15c563_05e9808c",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/TestNetworkService.java",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 201,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-05-13T11:20:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It is only sufficient if you unlock mTestNetworkTracker once after you\u0027ve set the member in the constructor.\n\nBelieve it or not, it\u0027s actually a common issue to see a member being null in another thread after it\u0027s been initialized to non-null in the constructor, because many developers don\u0027t understand that the guarantee that the fields are as fresh as the object only applies to final fields. Java 17.5.\n\nAs long as you have lock that\u0027s taken before it\u0027s read, and that lock is released at least once in the thread where the constructor is run after the write to the field, you should be okay. Locking before the read is not sufficient (the writing thread is under no obligation to have flushed its caches).",
      "parentUuid": "c19a841e_b1e6f67d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 201,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 201,
        "endChar": 66
      },
      "revId": "8d604fe6360528ab63c60f9e3ec9d7e9e96bd747",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
